(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["ec-easy-2026-014"]={"v":1,"id":"ec-easy-2026-014","title":"Mock Level Test-4 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 EC","sourceTitle":"Mock Level Test-4 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 EC","branch":"ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING","code":"EC","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2026 Online Test Series - Electronics Engineering","seriesId":"ec-easy-2026","num":14,"category":"mock","year":"2026","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Electronics Engineering • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Electronics Engineering"},"source":"ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING/MADE EASY/GATE_2026_+_GATE_2025_Online_Test_Series_Electronics_Engineering/026_Mock Level Test-4 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 EC.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider the below question followed by three statements. You have to study the question and the statements and decide which of the statement(s) is/are necessary to answer the given question.<br />\nA, B and C together start a business with a total investment of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/da/da91251fe33dbf1471e7.png\" /> At the end of the year, the total profit is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/22/2211c20705f88f1f7e1e.png\" /> What is A’s share in the profit?<br />\n1. A’s contribution is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/57/571a28b567c9698614a9.png\" /> times B’s contribution.<br />\n2. B’s contribution is twice that of C.<br />\n3. A’s contribution is thrice that of C.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"All 1, 2 and 3"},{"key":"D","html":"Any two of the three"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/91/91a49c0b45964e671d3e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":2,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Find the next term in the alpha-numerical series:<br />\nZ1A, X2D, V6G, T21J, R88M, P445P, ?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"N2676S"},{"key":"B","html":"N2676T"},{"key":"C","html":"T26TON"},{"key":"D","html":"T2676N"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c2/c24006aada2079c59084.png\" /></div>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Of the five villages P, Q, R, S and T situated close to each other, P is 1 m to the west of Q, R is 1 m to the south of P, T is 1 m to the north of Q and S is 1 m to the east of T. Then R is in which direction with respect to S?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"North-West"},{"key":"B","html":"South-East"},{"key":"C","html":"South-West"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d80606359c36474cd08a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A conical vessel whose internal radius is 10 cm and height 72 cm is full of water. If this water is poured into a cylindrical vessel with internal radius 30 cm, the height of the water level rises in it is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2f/2f8d9c4280fd58a7bb01.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/81/817475010e991c937c59.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/56/563cf7cb19a824372cbd.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6be0b3a7b62e983f7a1f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":5,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>An opaque solid cone is suspendended in the path of a parallel beam of light such that its shadow is cast on a screen oriented perpendicular to the direction of the light beam.<br />\nUnder these conditions, which one of the shadows <em>A</em>, <em>B</em>, <em>C</em> and <em>D</em> is not possible?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3c/3c74dd8bf2da97a6b6f5.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"A"},{"key":"B","html":"B"},{"key":"C","html":"C"},{"key":"D","html":"D"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\n&bull; A cone&rsquo;s circular base can project a circle when the cone&rsquo;s axis is perpendicular to the screen.<br />\n&bull; Tilt the cone a bit and the circle becomes an ellipse.<br />\n&bull; If the cone is oriented so the apex and base edge project on the screen, the outline can form a<br />\ntriangle C the lateral surface projects as two straight sloping edges meeting at the apex.</p>"},{"n":6,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The sum of all the numbers greater than 10000 formed by using digits 0, 2, 4, 6, 8 (no digit repeated in any number) is equal to?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"5199960"},{"key":"B","html":"5209960"},{"key":"C","html":"5199980"},{"key":"D","html":"5299960"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/16/16b716747e3f8daa98d3.png\" /></div>"},{"n":7,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Monica has a piece of canvas whose area is 551 m<sup>2</sup>. She uses it to have a conical tent made, with a base radius of 7 m. Assuming that all the stitching margins and the wastage incurred while cutting, amounts to approximately 1 m2, the volume of the tent is _____ m<sup>3</sup>.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1225,1239],"answerText":"1232","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1232 (1225 - 1239)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5d/5d44770e139a6e3f0d8b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":8,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The diameter of a sphere is decreased by 25%. By what percentage does its curved surface area decrease?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"25%"},{"key":"B","html":"37.5%"},{"key":"C","html":"43.75%"},{"key":"D","html":"50%"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nIf the diameter decreases by 25%, the radius also decreases by 25%.<br />\nSo the new radius = 75% of the old radius = 0.75r<br />\nCurved surface area is proportional to the square of the radius : (0.75)<sup>2</sup> = 0.5625<br />\nThis means the new area is 56.25% of the original area<br />\nSo, the decrease = 100 &ndash; 56.25 = 43.75%<br />\nTherefore, the curved surface area decreases by 43.75%.</p>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A tariff against computers made in country z is needed to protect computer manufactures in this country. With such a tariff, domestic computer manufactures would see increased sales of their own products. And increased sales frequently lead to reduced prices. The conclusion which can<br />\nbe most properly drawn from above statement is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"A lack of protective tariff has hampered computer production in this country."},{"key":"B","html":"A tariff would probably lead to a drop in prices for buyers of domestically produced computers."},{"key":"C","html":"Domestic manufacturers will decrease computer production if a protective tariff is not established"},{"key":"D","html":"A drop in computer prices is likely to create more jobs in the country."}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>"},{"n":10,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0","html":"<p>All the soldier are arranged in the form of an equivalent triangle i.e. one soldier in front row, 2 soldier in second row and 3 soldier in third row and so on. If 669 more soldiers from other are added in such a way that all the soldiers form a square and each of the side contains 8 less soldier<br />\nthan each side of equilateral triangle. The number of soldier initially were _________ .</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1540,1540],"answerText":"1540","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1540</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bb4ebe47b4757cc09620.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":11,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>If h[n] is a causal signal and <em>h</em>[<em>n</em>] = <em>h<sub>e</sub></em>[<em>n</em>] + <em>h<sub>o</sub></em>[<em>n</em>], then the expression for <em>h</em>[<em>n</em>] in terms of only <em>h<sub>o</sub></em>[<em>n</em>] is given by (where <em>h<sub>e</sub></em>[<em>n</em>] is even part of <em>h</em>[<em>n</em>] and ho[n] is odd part of <em>h</em>[<em>n</em>]).</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fd/fd5c499695c41aef5a7b.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5c/5c0dae510b2660bce001.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/71/719f90df42ba1be2fa1f.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d7/d745560e07eccba97275.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1c/1c6ad4c92480b6521c14.png\" /></div>"},{"n":12,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The generator matrix of a systematic (8, 4) linear block code is given by,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/40/40760dd68d918f988b75.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The minimum distance (<em>d</em><sub>min</sub>) of this code is __________.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[4,4],"answerText":"4","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>4 (4 - 4)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/77ae2a27b17c22fba058.png\" /></div>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The asymptotic bode magnitude plot of a minimum-phase transfer function <em>G</em>(<em>s</em>) is given below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/448a2a030b22b603c141.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The transfer function <em>G</em>(<em>s</em>) will be</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b0/b0dea10e4abb007a5114.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/28/2894d04d6b9d1827ec46.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/75/75452f95d608ae16d5e1.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/70/706648140857e5c92192.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c6/c682c856f0babfe8e9b2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider the state diagram of a sequential circuit as shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f0/f06ad9343ba5eef636f7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Assume that the circuit is in state-<em>A</em> initially. For which of the following sequence of input bits, the output will be equal to 1 for 3 times?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"100110101101000101"},{"key":"B","html":"110101101100010101"},{"key":"C","html":"111011101100101101"},{"key":"D","html":"10101011010101100"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/36/36d6378e920b15d230ca.png\" /></div>"},{"n":15,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following statements regarding ramp signal, <em>r</em>(<em>t</em>) and unit step signal, <em>u</em>(<em>t</em>) are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/9977faaa1c9a4230a2bc.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0b/0bea11046f4913a5b80b.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0a/0a466a4098a31a7d9ec4.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7c/7c72fc00edc684686c7e.png\" />"}],"answer":["A","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/36/3609d9ae176c26a7325f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":16,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A Si diode has a forward current of 2.5 mA, carrier life time τ = 100 ns and the maximum diffusion capacitance of 3 nF. With these specifications, Si diode is operating at a temperature of (Assume η = 2 for Si)</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"350 K"},{"key":"B","html":"483 K"},{"key":"C","html":"550 K"},{"key":"D","html":"623 K"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fd/fd453602022c1f6599cc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":17,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A heavily doped n-type semiconductor has the following data:<br />\nHole-electron mobility ratio = 0.50<br />\nDoping concentration <em>N<sub>D</sub></em> = 4.5 × 1015 cm<sup>–3</sup><br />\nIntrinsic concentration <em>n<sub>i</sub></em> = 1.5 × 1010 cm<sup>–3</sup><br />\nThen the ratio of conductivity of the n-type semiconductor to that of intrinsic semiconductor of<br />\nsame material is __________ × 10<sup>5</sup>.<br />\n[Assume that the operating temperature is same]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2 (2 - 2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/ea67a82c7b1d712ae892.png\" /></div>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A MOS capacitor is biased in such a way that the majority carriers in the semiconductor pile up at the oxide semiconductor interface. The device is biased in</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"accumulation region"},{"key":"B","html":"flat band region"},{"key":"C","html":"inversion region"},{"key":"D","html":"pinch-off region"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nIn accumulation mode, a gate voltage is applied at the MOSFET that attracts majority charge<br />\ncarriers from the bulk of the substrate towards the oxide-semiconductor interface.</p>"},{"n":19,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A 2 GHz standing wave pattern exists in a non-magnetic dielectric. If the distance between a maxima and its adjacent minima is 1.5 cm, then the value of relative permittivity (ε<em><sub>r</sub></em>) of the dielectric is equal to</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2.5"},{"key":"B","html":"6.25"},{"key":"C","html":"5"},{"key":"D","html":"5.35"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2d/2d10068905cc17e235b0.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/263e2dddfd1128ae4131.png\" /></div>"},{"n":20,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider the system shown below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/445ae1c2397ebc65a470.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The value of <em>K</em> for which the effect of step-disturbance <em>X</em>(<em>s</em>) on the output <em>Y</em>(<em>s</em>) will be minimum is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<em>K</em> = 0"},{"key":"B","html":"<em>K</em> should be small"},{"key":"C","html":"Independent of <em>K</em>"},{"key":"D","html":"<em>K</em> should be very large."}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fa/fad69cc6829142b9e38b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":21,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>If the eigen vectors of a 2 × 2 matrix A corresponding to the eigen values –1 and 6 are <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/40/4032f4f3993e60c33653.png\" /> and <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/8f/8fe939754bf75862a6b5.png\" /> respectively, then the matrix <em>A</em> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f4/f43849abbb90b0b6759d.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0d/0db15d60a95dbcec1af7.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fcc1dc92897438bbd689.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1f31c09301dc1b1e6df1.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d2/d2ae659fb187a3c2dea4.png\" /></div>"},{"n":22,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The particular solution of the differential equation</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2ed60676bd621b0994c6.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/ea06fab9243c991762a8.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/41/41ae1f204a6648d487c3.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/25/25fa637d45d64ace9367.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d5/d59f68b4503c60fdbd14.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/08/08aa7783aa3add8cf2a1.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/de/de96583f94f550bfb9b7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":23,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The open-loop transfer function of a system with unity negative feedback is given by,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/ecf5259801784c1e8273.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>For <em>K</em> = 2, the Nyquist plot of <em>G</em>(<em>s</em>) encircles the point (–1 + <em>j</em>0)</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"two times in clockwise direction"},{"key":"B","html":"two times in counterclockwise direction"},{"key":"C","html":"one time in clockwise direction"},{"key":"D","html":"one time in counterclockwise direction"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/28/28d144dcbc259a5493a8.png\" /></div>"},{"n":24,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider the following assembly language program of an 8085 microprocessor:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e7/e74a2a3f24d5a987fef7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The instruction stored at the location “LOOP” will be executed for</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"80 times"},{"key":"B","html":"50 times"},{"key":"C","html":"1 time"},{"key":"D","html":"Infinity times"}],"answer":["A","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C, A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nAfter &ldquo;XRA A&rdquo;, the content of the accumulator (A) will be &ldquo;00H&rdquo; and zero flag will set, irrespective<br />\nof the initial content of A.<br />\nSo, the instruction stored at the location &ldquo;LOOP&rdquo; will be executed only for one time.</p>"},{"n":25,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b7/b791036c1a390f5a7e63.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The diodes <em>D</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>D</em><sub>2</sub> are ideal and an input voltage of <em>v<sub>s</sub></em>(<em>t</em>) = 5sin(ω<em>t</em>) V is applied to the circuit. If the capacitors were initially discharged, then the value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d6/d6a14e721f64dac39a04.png\" /> under the steady-state condition is equal to</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2"},{"key":"B","html":"-1"},{"key":"C","html":"0.5"},{"key":"D","html":"-2"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/42/42e6f62886d761b91b69.png\" /></div>"},{"n":26,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the signal <em>x</em>(<em>t</em>) = cosπ<em>t</em> + <em>j</em>3sin(2π<em>t</em>). If this signal is represented as <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d6/d6c696784716859db841.png\" /> then <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/84/84b605d5c206b5c4d744.png\" /> is equal to ______. [Assume that ω<sub>0</sub> = 2π/<em>T</em> and <em>T</em> = fundamental period of x(t)]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3,3],"answerText":"3","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3 (3 - 3)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c6/c6d6c205bc0fa4e2954f.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c0/c0a1ee288138bf5254a3.png\" /></div>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The bandwidth of a single tone frequency modulated signal, according to the Carson’s rule, is 150 kHz. If the frequency of the message signal is increased by 5 kHz by keeping all other parameters constant, then the bandwidth of the new FM signal will be ___________ kHz.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[159,161],"answerText":"160","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>160 (159 - 161)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/66/669ae39c68081035ee15.png\" /></div>"},{"n":28,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the digital circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8f/8f84de0bf566d50986ff.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Assuming that the flip-flops have no propagation delay and the NOT gates are designed to have a propagation delay of 3 ns, then the output frequency at Q<sub>2</sub> is equal to _________ MHz. (upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5.5,7.5],"answerText":"6.94","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>6.94 (5.50 - 7.50)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1f99e1e7699e9ed982c1.png\" /></div>"},{"n":29,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the magnitude and phase response of a certain DTFT system shown below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6f/6f79d27fd8ea761686ef.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Then the inverse DTFT system has samples at</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0 and 1"},{"key":"B","html":"1 and –1"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"–1 and 0"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/48/489f7e806791ba3bc014.png\" /></div>"},{"n":30,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The minimum number of <em>J</em>-<em>K</em> flip-flops required to design a Mealy type overlapping sequence detector, which produces output 1 if the input sequence is either 1100 or 1111, is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2"},{"key":"B","html":"3"},{"key":"C","html":"4"},{"key":"D","html":"5"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4b/4b009e715ee309d8d5ee.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/ecb9f19d0098a61b5c00.png\" /></div>"},{"n":31,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the characteristic equation:<br />\n2<em>s</em><sup>5</sup> + <em>s</em><sup>4</sup> + 4<em>s</em><sup>3</sup> + 2<em>s</em><sup>2</sup> + 2<em>s</em> + 1 = 0<br />\nThe number of roots that lie in the left half of s-plane is ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1,1],"answerText":"1","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1 (1 - 1)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c2/c22587d17cd39ca7fc68.png\" /></div>"},{"n":32,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the networks shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fd/fdfa40ee42d45282640f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If the networks given in figure-1 and figure-2 offer same impedance across the terminals <em>a</em> and <em>b</em> at ω = 1 rad/sec, then the values of R and L of the network shown in figure-2 will be respectively</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<em>R</em> = 2 Ω and <em>L</em> = 1 H"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a8/a80ce18d83ab83f22ddb.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<em>R</em> = 1 Ω and <em>L</em> = 1 H"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c8/c8d1be2653af09393750.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b3/b398cd3a720e85dd7e0f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":33,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In the circuit shown below, the voltage <em>V</em><sub>0</sub> across 5 Ω resistor is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/41/415a7bd161e77531137d.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"28.92 V"},{"key":"B","html":"57.84 V"},{"key":"C","html":"40.90 V"},{"key":"D","html":"81.82 V"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ac/ac1ed840b8e65d14c2f9.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/74/7458a70ed8179045acf6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":34,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider a threshold comparator with input <em>R</em> = <em>X</em> + <em>N</em>. Where, <em>X</em> is the signal level at the input of the comparator due to transmitted binary data and it takes the values “+1” and “–1” with probabilities 1/3 and 2/3 respectively. N is a uniformly distributed noise variable with a variance of 3. The mean of the noise variable is βX. The threshold value (rth) of the comparator is decided in an optimum way using maximum a posteriori (MAP) criteria. If β = 0.50, then the probability of error resulting in the decision made by the comparator will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/21/212042cf645a211835d6.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/16/160ef4f5a5a39f4987dd.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/45/454dde5e1cd3c3b1386f.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b7/b756b7a6697b50d0f1b6.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"},{"n":35,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A random variable is defined by</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fd/fd06879fe56c57548a04.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The expected value of 2x + 5 is _______.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[7,7],"answerText":"7","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>7</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/72/72163d1782e26fd4221c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":36,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The amplitude of a stationary random signal <em>X</em>(<em>t</em>) is uniformly distributed in the range [–5, 5]. The samples of this signal are applied to a quantizer, whose input (<em>X</em>) – output (<em>Y</em>) characteristics are given as follows:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/83db154f5fba5f0e1809.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The signal power-to-quantization noise power ratio at the output of the quantizer, corresponding to the message signal <em>X</em>(<em>t</em>), is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"10.55 dB"},{"key":"B","html":"12.04 dB"},{"key":"C","html":"13.80 dB"},{"key":"D","html":"15.20 dB"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/71/715fe9d47244c13bf3fd.png\" /></div>"},{"n":37,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the Zener voltage regulator circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/05/05b9b3ae17df98684005.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If the value of Zener voltage <em>V<sub>Z</sub></em> = 15 V, then the value of load current <em>I<sub>L</sub></em> is equal to ________ mA.<br />\n(upto one decimal place)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[177,179],"answerText":"177.8","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>177.8 (177.0 - 179.0)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9b/9b62968c467f35d67085.png\" /></div>"},{"n":38,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ed/edf6f6ef4b5428e73185.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The transistors <em>Q</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>Q</em><sub>2</sub> have small signal transconductances <em>g</em><sub><em>m</em>1</sub> and <em>g</em><sub><em>m</em>2</sub> respectively. Assume that both the transistors are working in active region with negligible effect of base width modulation. Then the value of small signal voltage gain Av is equal to [Assume β to be large for both the transistors]</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ef/efc629d0c2e32a1d42dc.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6be0c3aecdaf86d0e680.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/dd/dda1289c4630d1dc5cd8.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3a/3ac36c95c412d724edcd.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2e49002699882b816874.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/89/895fa025429c5cde9c37.png\" /></div>\n</div>"},{"n":39,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the transistor circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f676a1ed406e8fe6e651.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The circuit consists of an N-MOS transistor with <em>V<sub>TN</sub></em> = 2 V,<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/777a823a7ca8fd667d50.png\" /> If the transistor is operated at a D.C. voltage of 10 V, then the power dissipated across the transistor is equal to</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1.72 mW"},{"key":"B","html":"2.35 mW"},{"key":"C","html":"3.56 mW"},{"key":"D","html":"4.70 mW"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a9/a94e3a4ac73d8e99647f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":40,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the circuit shown below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/96/96a5cb73039ab0260494.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The value of <em>R</em> that will result in maximum power transfer to it will be _________ Ω. (upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.65,0.69],"answerText":"0.67","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.67 (0.65 - 0.69)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ab/aba99ebf8c426e1a43b9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":41,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the op-amp circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/04/0459f122861323ba2b96.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Assume the op-amp to be ideal. The value of voltage gain <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/9f/9f2f0b8aba0883b35d22.png\" /> of the amplifier is _______ V/V.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-8,-8],"answerText":"-8","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-8 (-8 - -8)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c1/c1e7c82be6acb61d7014.png\" /></div>"},{"n":42,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the system shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/76/76ace808fe77ebbd8d44.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The steady state error of this system is defined as, <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/f0/f00ac659c2cef15c060e.png\" /> If the system is excited with a unit step input, then the resulting steady state error will be __________.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.74,0.76],"answerText":"0.75","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.75 (0.74 - 0.76)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fcea7267fff59a7d5c8f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":43,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The electric field component of a wave travelling in free space is given by,</p>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bc/bc8bab68e12544778412.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The frequency of the wave is _________ × 10<sup>10</sup> rad/sec</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.8,2],"answerText":"1.5","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.5 (0.8 - 2.0)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0d/0d9b2bee027fb47ec698.png\" /></div>"},{"n":44,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Let <em>x</em>[<em>n</em>] be a finite length sequence given by <em>x</em>[<em>n</em>] = {1, 2, A, 1, 3, 2} whose DFT is <em>X</em>[<em>k</em>]. If the value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/89/8986a5d7405222c416a6.png\" /> then the value of ‘<em>A</em>’ is ___________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0,0],"answerText":"0","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2b/2be9227c29e1b2ba7fab.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5d/5db1be3c83e8fbc3328a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":45,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Let <em>X</em> be a discrete memoryless source producing “n” different alphabets {<em>A</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>A</em><sub>2</sub>, ......, An} with probabilities {<em>p</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>p</em><sub>2</sub>, .... , <em>p</em><sub>n</sub>} respectively. Another discrete memoryless source Y is designed such that it produces words each with 3 alphabets produced by X, i.e. “Y = X ⋅ X ⋅ X”. If the entropy of<em> X</em> is <em>H</em>(<em>X</em>) = 4 bits/symbol, then the entropy of Y will be ___________ bits/word.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[11.5,12.5],"answerText":"12","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>12 (11.5 - 12.5)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/85/85da16ac79b53a73a1fc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":46,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The range of address that can be used to access the memory (RAM) in the below figure is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f3/f34905e14d14a544583e.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"6000H to 7FFFH"},{"key":"B","html":"6000H to 7FFEH"},{"key":"C","html":"E000H to EFFFH"},{"key":"D","html":"E000H to EFFEH"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/02/02e4b027421e0cdeb273.png\" /></div>"},{"n":47,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The directional derivative of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi</annotation></semantics> </math> </span></span></span>(<em>x</em>, y, z) = <em>xy</em><sup>2</sup><em>z</em> + 4yz<sup>2</sup> at the point <em>P</em>(1, 2, –1) along <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/55/55c397604611dadb9a91.png\" /> is</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-6.6,-6.4],"answerText":"-6.532","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-6.532 (-6.600 - -6.400)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/21/21de41b1ce20e7f4799d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":48,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>If <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) = 12<em>x</em><sup>5</sup> – 45<em>x</em><sup>4</sup> – 20<em>x</em><sup>3</sup> + 90<em>x</em><sup>2</sup>, then</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The minimum value of the function <em>f</em>(<em>x</em>) is 0."},{"key":"B","html":"The maximum value of the function <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) is 53."},{"key":"C","html":"<em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) has neither a maximum nor a minimum at <em>x</em> = –1."},{"key":"D","html":"<em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) has neither a maximum nor a minimum at x = 3."}],"answer":["A","B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6bbde512a2a920546fc5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":49,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In a coherent BPSK system, equiprobable bits are modelled as,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/77002110a2839d488701.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Here <em>f<sub>c</sub></em> is selected as the integer multiple of 1/<em>T<sub>b</sub></em> and <em>T<sub>b</sub></em> is the duration of each bit. The modulated signal is transmitted through an AWGN channel, with two-sided noise power spectral density of N<sub>0</sub>/2. In addition to the additive noise, the channel also offers an attenuation of 1 dB/km to the signal component. At the output of the channel, the signal is received by the receiver shown<br />\nbelow.\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/6e/6e21440bb2ff017d6356.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The channel length is 10 km and the probability of error achieved by the system is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/3b/3b21f395172681309bcb.png\" />The value of “β” is __________.\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a1/a12d1d93f2b034038c80.png\" /></div>\n</div>\n</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.08,0.12],"answerText":"0.10","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.10 (0.08 - 0.12)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d7/d778572524f77849ae32.png\" /></div>"},{"n":50,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In the circuit shown below, the network N contains only resistors.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d8d8e006a9a4f8ac7892.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If <em>E</em> = 5 V and <em>I</em> is replaced by a 2 Ω resistor, then the voltage <em>V</em><sub>0</sub> is ______________ V.</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2 (2 - 2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cc/cc702fff25fe499be8e4.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/72/721cbdf958a27ddc831a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":51,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b3/b3ab582961021fe8c938.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If the transistor is biased in saturation region with <em>g<sub>m</sub></em> = 1.57 mA/V, then the value of small signal voltage gain  <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/11/117206a0fb655be3eb7d.png\" /> is equal to ___________ V/V. (Assume λ = 0) [Answer upto two decimal places]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-3.75,-3.5],"answerText":"-3.62","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-3.62 (-3.75 - -3.50)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c1/c13b79f0d1cff3e2f369.png\" /></div>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A <em>p</em><sup>+</sup><em>n</em> abrupt junction has a built-in potential of 0.8 V. The depletion layer width at a reverse bias voltage (magnitude) of 1.2 V is 1.5 μm. For a reverse bias voltage 7.5 V, the depletion layer width will be ________ μm. (upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.95,3.16],"answerText":"3.06","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3.06 (2.95 - 3.16)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/267af17ad361bd45eb6c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":53,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Let <em>y</em>[<em>n</em>] denote the convolution of <em>h</em>[<em>n</em>] and <em>x</em>[<em>n</em>], where <em>h</em>[<em>n</em>] = <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f68f6880b0ed4c11bc50.png\" /> and <em>x</em>[<em>n</em>] is a causal sequence. If y[0] = 1/2 and y[1] = 1, then <em>x</em>[1] equal to _________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.5,1],"answerText":"0.875","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.875 (0.50 - 1.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e3/e3bee4bd4e1c19147751.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/18807acf181b3d03525c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":54,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the electrical network shown in the figure below along with its state equation:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/26059bd613db7ee5d0c3.png\" />\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1e/1e047da9ecafa6381a74.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The state matrix <em>A</em> is equal to</div>\n</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e3/e3591d2416183ac8de7f.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/ea0e0c6cce9899fce856.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/57/574c99d8a07d5105798a.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/06/06fe75937471996c0685.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1c/1c2b0230414d7ba02ca3.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/43/43b6a45ad769679f1de6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":55,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the following Boolean expression:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bd/bd8749921162181427f2.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The minimum number of two-input NAND gates required to construct the above circuit is equal to ___________.<br />\n[Assume that only uncomplemented form of inputs are available]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[8,8],"answerText":"8","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>8 (8 - 8)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/73/73ab2d5e6c5f264cd214.png\" /></div>"},{"n":56,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The reflection coefficient at the load end, of a 500 m transmission line, has a phase angle of “–150°”. If the operating wavelength is 150 m, then the total number of voltage maxima on the line is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"5"},{"key":"B","html":"6"},{"key":"C","html":"7"},{"key":"D","html":"8"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c6/c6c6aa7afe07c18be5f6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":57,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>An ideal MOS capacitor with p-type substrate has an oxide layer with thickness of 1.8 μm and the ratio ε<em><sub>si</sub></em> / ε<em><sub>ox</sub></em> = 3. Due to the application of the gate voltage, a surface potential of 0.035 V has been developed at the semiconductor-oxide layer interface, and a depletion region of width 0.4 μm is created inside the semiconductor. The gate voltage applied is<br />\n(Assume that the source and body terminals are grounded)</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0.98 V"},{"key":"B","html":"2.035 V"},{"key":"C","html":"0.735 V"},{"key":"D","html":"0.335 V"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5e2e2f17fb92d14bf3e7.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e8/e825ffdbe73c3344190c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":58,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>An electromagnetic wave has the electric field intensity in phasor form, <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/f4/f49ed6f54106af554eec.png\" /></p>\n\n<p>The EM wave is incident on a perfect conducting surface located at y = 0. The reflected wave is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"left hand circularly polarized"},{"key":"B","html":"right hand circularly polarized"},{"key":"C","html":"linearly polarized"},{"key":"D","html":"left hand elliptically polarized"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5a/5aace08a63dab04edff2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":59,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the difference equation of a digital filter shown below:<br />\ny[n] = x[n – 1] – ay[n – 1]<br />\nIf this filter’s frequency response has a value of 0.25 at ω = 0, then the value of frequency response at ω = π rad/s will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0.5"},{"key":"B","html":"1"},{"key":"C","html":"1.5"},{"key":"D","html":"2"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d7/d77bd5b48cf8404ee424.png\" /></div>"},{"n":60,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The output of a digital circuit is expressed by the following Boolean function:</p>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6d/6d878e50972cff9b5406.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Which of the following statements are correct?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The output is always high if <em>B</em> = 0 and <em>C</em> = 1"},{"key":"B","html":"The output is always high if <em>A</em> = 1, <em>B</em> = 0 and <em>C</em> = 1"},{"key":"C","html":"The output is always high if <em>C</em> = 1 and <em>D</em> = 1"},{"key":"D","html":"The output is always high if <em>A</em> = 0 and <em>B</em> = 0"}],"answer":["A","B","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/12/12dd9736e89b67f34047.png\" /></div>"},{"n":61,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the common base BJT circuit shown below with β = 99 and <em>V<sub>A</sub></em> = ∞ at room temperature.<br />\n(Assume <em>V<sub>T</sub></em> = 26 mV)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/80/8075c68e6c9caf70ae41.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Choose the correct statements:</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Input resistance, <em>R</em><sub>in</sub> = 78 Ω"},{"key":"B","html":"Voltage gain, <em>A<sub>V</sub></em> = 90.5"},{"key":"C","html":"Input resistance, <em>R</em><sub>in</sub> = 178 Ω"},{"key":"D","html":"Voltage gain, <em>A<sub>V</sub></em> = 9.56"}],"answer":["A","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/04/042f140ded0ce2587287.png\" /></div>"},{"n":62,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A 50 Ω transmission line is first short circuited and the minima locations are observed. When this short circuit is replaced by a resistive load <em>R<sub>L</sub></em>, the VSWR is 5. If the locations of the minima are same in both the cases, then the value of load resistance <em>R<sub>L</sub></em> will be __________ Ω.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[9,11],"answerText":"10","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>10 (9 - 11)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2eca2ad8cdaabad66962.png\" /></div>"},{"n":63,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider an analytic function <em>f</em> (<em>z</em>) = <em>u</em> + <em>i ν</em>, if it is given than<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/cb/cbfde1d918b7e1e35c88.png\" />is a constant, then which of the following statements are true?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ef/ef7459520e0e291609aa.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"(i) and (ii) only"},{"key":"B","html":"(i) and (iii) only"},{"key":"C","html":"(ii) and (ii) only"},{"key":"D","html":"all are correct"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/be/be107d3eab00a535b8b1.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/52/52748e9c702873b86e21.png\" /></div>"},{"n":64,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A function <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) is defined as <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/0c/0ce4af0e7bd5c94b557b.png\" /></p>\n\n<p>For <em>f</em>(<em>x</em>) to be a valid probability density function the value of <em>A</em> must be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"8"},{"key":"B","html":"16"},{"key":"C","html":"18"},{"key":"D","html":"22"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/3468ed55670c692c7342.png\" /></div>"},{"n":65,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>If the residue of the function <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/b6/b625498475c443baca2e.png\" /> then the value of <em>p</em> is ______.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/69/69e89f7a349817dc0322.png\" /></div>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":35,"NAT":25,"MSQ":5},"withoutKey":0}};
